# Copy to .env and fill in the values you need. The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix is
# required for Expo to inline these into the client bundle. Everything here is
# public config only; no secret ever belongs in this file or the app bundle.

# --- Auth Worker (Cloudflare) -------------------------------------------------
#
# The deployed better-auth Worker the app talks to. Defaults to the live URL in
# lib/authClient.ts, so this is only needed to point at a local `wrangler dev`
# (http://127.0.0.1:8787) or a staging Worker.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_AUTH_URL=https://pusoy-now-auth.fullvaluedan.workers.dev

# --- Provider setup (no secret belongs in this file) --------------------------
#
# Google and Facebook client ids/secrets are NOT app config: they are wrangler
# secrets on the auth Worker, set with `wrangler secret put` from server/. The
# app never sees them. See docs/AUTH-SETUP.md for the exact console steps and
# the redirect URIs to register.
#
# The same goes for the other Worker secrets (verification email, captcha,
# Stripe): all live on the Worker, never here. Nothing about enabling a provider
# requires a value in this file.

# --- TikTok (deferred) --------------------------------------------------------
#
# TikTok is not a better-auth provider; it needs its own Login Kit bridge on the
# Worker (deferred). The client key below is public and only starts the Login
# Kit flow. The client SECRET lives on the server side, never here.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=your-tiktok-client-key
